Package: LODI
Type: Package
Title: LOngitudinal Dynamic Interaction Model for Microbiome Count Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Shuangjie", "Zhang", email = "shuangjie.zhang@austin.utexas.edu",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A Bayesian dynamic factor model for longitudinal microbiome count
    data. LODI models the observed counts through a rounded multivariate
    log-normal kernel and decomposes the within-subject temporal signal into a
    per-feature drift term (a genotype-specific AR(1) process with a
    Dirichlet-process mixture prior on the initial baseline) and a shared
    cross-feature factor term (a static loading matrix paired with an AR(1)
    latent factor process). This decomposition yields a time-indexed
    cross-feature covariance and separates individual taxon trajectories from
    the shared dynamics that drive interactions. The loading matrix is
    identified via the standard lower-triangular constraint with positive
    diagonal. Methods are described in Zhang, Ok, and Ni (submitted),
    "Bayesian Nonparametric Longitudinal Factor Model for Microbiome Counts."
